--- !u!114 &1201976299
MonoBehaviour:
  m_ObjectHideFlags: 0
  m_CorrespondingSourceObject: {fileID: 0}
  m_PrefabInstance: {fileID: 0}
  m_PrefabAsset: {fileID: 0}
  m_GameObject: {fileID: 1201976297}
  m_Enabled: 1
  m_EditorHideFlags: 0
  m_Script: {fileID: 11500000, guid: f4688fdb7df04437aeb418b961361dc5, type: 3}
  m_Name: 
  m_EditorClassIdentifier: Unity.TextMeshPro::TMPro.TextMeshProUGUI
  m_Material: {fileID: 0}
  m_Color: {r: 1, g: 1, b: 1, a: 1}
  m_RaycastTarget: 1
  m_RaycastPadding: {x: 0, y: 0, z: 0, w: 0}
  m_Maskable: 1
  m_OnCullStateChanged:
    m_PersistentCalls:
      m_Calls: []
  m_text: "\u2014 GENERAL INFORMATION \u2014\n\nClass - Your character's profession
    or vocation. It determines your special abilities, combat style, and magic. (e.g.,
    A Wizard casts spells, a Fighter uses weapons).\n\nLevel - A measurement of your
    character's overall power and experience. All adventurers start at Level 1. The
    higher the level, the tougher the challenges you can face.\n\nRace - Your character's
    species and heritage. Your race determines your physical appearance, age, and
    natural talents (such as seeing in the dark or resisting magic).\n\n\u2014 ABILITY
    SCORES (STATS) \u2014\n\nStrength (STR) - Measures physical power and athletic
    training. It determines how hard you hit with melee weapons, how much you can
    carry, and how well you can break down doors or grapple enemies.\n\nDexterity
    (DEX) - Measures agility, reflexes, and balance. It determines your Armor Class
    (how hard you are to hit), initiative (how fast you react in combat), and accuracy
    with ranged weapons (like bows).\n\nConstitution (CON) - Measures health, stamina,
    and vital force. It determines your Hit Points (HP)\u2014how much damage you
    can take before falling unconscious.\n\nIntelligence (INT) - Measures mental
    acuity, information recall, and analytical skill. It is the primary stat for
    Wizards and is used to recall lore or investigate clues.\n\nWisdom (WIS) - Measures
    awareness, intuition, and willpower. Unlike Intelligence (book smarts), Wisdom
    is \"street smarts\" and senses. It helps you perceive hidden enemies or resist
    mind control.\n\nCharisma (CHA) - Measures confidence, eloquence, and leadership.
    It represents your force of personality. It is used to persuade, intimidate,
    or deceive others.\n\n\u2014 SAVING THROWS \u2014 \n\nA specific reaction to
    resist a harmful effect. While an \"Attack\" is you hitting an enemy, a \"Saving
    Throw\" is you preventing an enemy from affecting you.\n\nSTR Save: Resisting
    being pushed or toppled.\n\nDEX Save: Dodging a fireball or falling rock.\n\nCON
    Save: Resisting poison or disease.\n\nINT Save: Resisting psychic attacks.\n\nWIS
    Save: Resisting mind control or fear.\n\nCHA Save: Resisting banishment or possession.\n\n\u2014
    SKILLS \u2014\n\nAcrobatics (Dexterity): Staying on your feet on slippery ice,
    balancing on a tightrope, or breaking out of a grapple.\n\nAnimal Handling (Wisdom):
    Calming a spooked horse, intuiting an animal's intentions, or controlling a mount.\n\nArcana
    (Intelligence): Your ability to recall lore about spells, magic items, eldritch
    symbols, and magical traditions.\n\nAthletics (Strength): Climbing steep cliffs,
    jumping long distances, or swimming through rough currents.\n\nDeception (Charisma):
    Hiding the truth, whether verbally or through actions. Includes lying and conning.\n\nHistory
    (Intelligence): Recalling lore about historical events, legendary people, ancient
    kingdoms, and lost wars.\n\nInsight (Wisdom): Determining the true intentions
    of a creature, such as detecting a lie or predicting someone\u2019s next move.\n\nIntimidation
    (Charisma): Influencing someone through overt threats, hostile actions, or physical
    violence.\n\nInvestigation (Intelligence): Looking for clues and making deductions
    based on them. Used to find hidden objects or deduce how a mechanism works.\n\nMedicine
    (Wisdom): Stabilizing a dying companion or diagnosing an illness.\n\nNature (Intelligence):
    Recalling lore about terrain, plants and animals, the weather, and natural cycles.\n\nPerception
    (Wisdom): Spotting, hearing, or detecting the presence of something. Used to
    find hidden enemies or eavesdrop.\n\nReligion (Intelligence): Recalling lore
    about deities, rites and prayers, religious hierarchies, and holy symbols.\n\nSleight
    of Hand (Dexterity): Planting an object on someone, concealing a coin, or picking
    a pocket.\n\nStealth (Dexterity): Concealing yourself from enemies, slinking
    through shadows, and moving silently.\n\nSurvival (Wisdom): Following tracks,
    hunting wild game, guiding a group through frozen wastelands, or identifying
    signs of owlbears."
  m_isRightToLeft: 0
